{"seq":4,"id":"01M6PN9BE9HK2FV1Z5VT58KY53","cdr":"CDR-0006","attempt":"CDR-0006-A1","type":"agent.result","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"test_author","adapter":"claude"},"at":"2026-11-05T20:09:30.313Z","payload":{"role":"test_author","adapter":"claude","result_sha256":"856c60e76cbacf3c6cced6691815b423150cb22a28845ff51ec8d7c1bb112de2","result":{"tests":[{"path":"makefile_cdr0006_test.go","covers_criterion":"All five criteria: TestMakefileExistsAtRoot (a Makefile exists at the repository root); TestMakeTestRunsGoTest (`make test` runs `go test ./...`); TestMakeVetRunsGoVet (`make vet` runs `go vet ./...`); TestMakeDefaultRunsTestAndVet (`make` with no target runs both); TestTestAndVetArePhony (`test` and `vet` are declared .PHONY)."}],"run_command":"go test .","notes":"I did not run these tests because this role has no shell. By inspection, all five should fail on the current code because there is no Makefile.\n\nThe test file is at the repository root in `package toy`. The README lists only the `cache`, `ledger`, `parse` and `report` packages, so I assumed the root has no Go package, but I could not list the directory to confirm it. If a root package with another name exists, the package clause must change.\n\nThe tests use `make -n`, so recipes are never executed and `make test` does not recurse into these tests. For the same reason, do not use a `+` prefix on the `go test` recipe, because `make -n` would execute it and recurse.\n\nRecipes must contain the literal strings `go test ./...` and `go vet ./...`. A `@` prefix is fine, because `make -n` still prints the command without it.\n\nThe .PHONY check is behavioural. It copies the Makefile to a temp dir next to files named `test` and `vet`, then expects the recipes to still print.\n\n`make` must be on PATH. If it is missing, the tests fail rather than skip."}},"cost":{"tokens_in":8,"tokens_out":4689,"tokens_cache_write":17940,"tokens_cache_read":13912,"seconds":49.266067041,"usd":0.24011439999999998},"signer":"ads-t